# Day 2 - Titanic Survival Prediction

## Overview
This project uses Machine Learning to predict whether a passenger survived the Titanic disaster.

## Dataset
Titanic Survival Dataset

## Algorithm
Logistic Regression

## Features Used
- Pclass
- Age
- Fare

## Target Variable
- Survived

## Tools & Libraries
- Python
- Pandas
- Scikit-learn
- Google Colab

## Workflow
1. Load dataset
2. Handle missing values
3. Select features
4. Split data into training and testing sets
5. Train Logistic Regression model
6. Evaluate model performance
7. Predict survival for a new passenger

## Results
- Accuracy: 73.74%
- Generated Confusion Matrix for evaluation

## Learning Outcome
Learned the basics of:
- Data preprocessing
- Binary classification
- Logistic Regression
- Model evaluation using accuracy and confusion matrix
